My LlamaIndex Agent vs LangChain Agent

LangChain is built around LLM reasoning. It decides which tools to calls and act on results. RAG is a tool for LangChain. 

LlamaIndex is a RAG framework that supports agents. Chunking, node relationships, retrieval modes, etc are configured easily. 

LangChain I built was able to answer out of scope questions with ease, knowing when to skip the retrieval tool. I had to configure the LlamaIndex agent specifically with system prompt to have it selectively use the retreival tool after I exposed as a tool. 

LLamaIndex seems to be more useful wehn the focus is on querying data. Different data sources can added or swapped with ease on LlamaIndex while more explicit configuration is needed with LangChain. 
